v0.9.0

Features and improvements
  - SOUND! every sound effect comes out of the loaded WAD, with the original's
    own attenuation, stereo panning, channel priorities and random pitch wobble
    - add-ons can replace individual sounds, in the original DMX format or as
      Ogg/WAV/FLAC; a sound the WAD set lacks is silent rather than substituted
    - volume slider on the start menu (remembered between sessions), M mutes
  - player movement more like vanilla
    - straferunning works
    - the player slides along angled walls instead of sticking to them
    - improved auto-aim
  - completed mancubus, arch-vile, revenant and pain elemental attacks
    - monster melee/ranged damage now matches vanilla's real dice instead of a
      softer tuned approximation
  - the cyberdemon's rocket splashes like the player's own
  - monster projectile speeds are vanilla's own now instead of eyeballed
  - monsters keep infighting when the player dies
  - the BFG now deals its real vanilla damage instead of a plain radius
    splash, complete with the green flash on whatever each ray hits
  - projectiles, explosions, teleport fog and the revenant's smoke trail are
    batched like map things now instead of one draw call each
  - add error message if WebGL2 is not available / unable to initialize

Fixed bugs
  - fixed monster fireballs flying straight through their own species instead
    of harmlessly exploding on it
  - fixed closing doors could trap the player (or a monster) underneath instead
    of bumping back open
  - lifts, rising floors (including stairs) and non-crushing ceiling movers now
    stop instead of clipping through the player or a monster
  - explosions no longer damage the spider mastermind or cyberdemon
  - fixed a crash (frozen game) whenever a monster's attack-pose animation was
    still playing at the moment it resumed walking — only reachable by the
    arch-vile so far, but the underlying bug was in the shared sprite animator
  - fixed monster projectiles damaging through walls
  - fixed dead lost souls/pain elementals leaving a permanent floating corpse
    instead of vanishing

===============================================================================

v0.8.0
Gameplay
  - all powerups work now: invulnerability, berserk, partial invisibility,
    radiation suit, computer area map and light amp visor, on vanilla's timers
    (incl. screen tints for invulnerability/suit, and monsters shooting wide
    while you're invisible)
  - backpack works now, and was invisible before (doomednum 8 had no sprite)
  - fist and chainsaw finally do damage (2-20, x10 for the fist with berserk)
Engine
  - MASSIVE performance optimizations (NUTS.WAD from ~2 fps to ~38 fps !!!)
  - add support for A LOT more linedef/sector specials! 
    Vanilla compatiblity should be complete now.
  - add attack & pain animations
  - improved lightning, we're now much closer to vanilla
  - wall/floor "fading" effect now also applies to awake monsters (still needs some tweaking)
  - fixed useable linedefs could be triggered from both sides
  - fixed a monster teleporting through a walk trigger ended up facing the
    wrong way (its landing angle got converted from degrees a second time)
  - fixed picking wrong player1 spawn if multiple player1 spawns are present
UI / HUD
  - new HUD strip showing which powerups are running and for how much longer
  - more accurate FPS counter
  - DEVMODE: add simple profiler overlay

